# Backend conventions

- Organize new code by business capability (Bookings, Pricing, Customers, …) when that phase starts. Do not create empty module folders early.
- Do not apply the Repository pattern by default; use EF Core directly unless an abstraction earns its keep.
- Controllers: HTTP and DTO mapping only.
- Return ProblemDetails for errors.
- Enforce authorization on the server.
- Pricing logic belongs in the API, never in a frontend.
- Assignment of vehicles must be transactional and safe under concurrency (see `docs/database/database-design.md`).
- No payment namespace, controllers, or EF entities.
- After API changes: `dotnet test BangaloreTaxi.sln`.
- Cross-cutting pipeline code lives in `Hosting/`. Business modules get their own folders only when that phase starts.
